usb: gadget: configfs: bind functions that configfs linked

On the Samsung/Exynos gadget, CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_UEVENT puts every
configfs-linked function on gi->linked_func instead of cfg->func_list,
and only the "adb" special case in config_usb_cfg_link() ever moves one
into a configuration. configfs_composite_bind() then walks cfg->func_list
alone, so any other function never reaches usb_add_function(), never gets
its ->bind(), and the gadget either starts without it or fails:

  Config b/1 of g1 needs at least one function.
  configfs-gadget 13600000.dwc3: failed to start g1: -22

For f_hid that means hidg_bind() never runs, so /dev/hidg0 is never
created and Kali NetHunter's USB Arsenal (which writes the gadget through
configfs and then checks /dev/hidg0) reports "Failed to set USB function."

Move whatever is staged on gi->linked_func into the configuration that is
about to be bound, before the "at least one function" check. Behaviour for
the GSI adb path is unchanged: adb was already moved there by the special
case, and everything configfs linked to the gadget now actually attaches.
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c	2026-11-14 12:56:10
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c	2026-11-14 12:56:10
@@ -1648,6 +1648,31 @@
 	}
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_UEVENT
+	/*
+	 * Functions linked through configfs are parked on gi->linked_func and,
+	 * in stock Samsung code, only the "adb" special case below ever moves
+	 * one into a configuration. Everything else (f_hid, for example) stays
+	 * stranded there, never reaches usb_add_function() and therefore never
+	 * binds: no /dev/hidg0, and the gadget start fails with -EINVAL once the
+	 * configuration ends up empty. Attach whatever configfs linked to the
+	 * configuration that is about to be bound.
+	 */
+	if (!list_empty(&gi->linked_func)) {
+		struct usb_configuration *cfg_c;
+		struct config_usb_cfg *cf;
+		struct usb_function *sf, *stmp;
+
+		cfg_c = list_first_entry_or_null(&gi->cdev.configs,
+						 struct usb_configuration, list);
+		if (cfg_c) {
+			cf = container_of(cfg_c, struct config_usb_cfg, c);
+			list_for_each_entry_safe(sf, stmp, &gi->linked_func, list)
+				list_move_tail(&sf->list, &cf->func_list);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 	list_for_each_entry(c, &gi->cdev.configs, list) {
 		struct config_usb_cfg *cfg;
 
